{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129278-please-educate-me-on-obfuscate","id":1129278,"title":"Please educate me on Obfuscate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-15T09:57:51-07:00","id":1129278,"title":"Please educate me on Obfuscate","content":"Suddenly, I have a bunch of players having Ofuscate and some problems about the nuances. Maybe you can help\u00fc me understand. It resolves mostly about Ofuscate 1, but I got questions for 2 and 3 as well..<br /> <br /> So, the eyes slide off the Vampire, I understand that. And they can\u00b4t really describe me, if they must. But what if I am in a place where I don\u00b4t belong? Let\u00b4s say, someone comes into his private bedroom and there is an Obfuscated Vampire. What happens? Does Obfuscate fail or will he roll Wits + Composure - Obfuscate. And if he fails that roll, what then? Does he sees &quot;someone&quot; but can\u00b4t remember him? Or does he sees someone and recognizes him until he went out of the room and then his memory is clouded?<br /> And when he comes into his room, makes his roll and fails, what happens when that Vampire talks with him. Does he talk to someone he does not recognize? What happens if he knows that Vampire he\u00b4s speaking to? Would he not recognize him?<br /> <br /> And the about Obfuscate 2: I have got a rule: When in games an ability looks particularly weak there\u00b4s a great chance that you haven\u00b4t understood it. I mean, carrying stuff around can be done with 1. So it\u00b4s only really useful when you cloud an object that you aren\u00b4t touching. But since it only begins to work when you touch it and it only is active for a scene, you must be present and touch this thing before. I can imagine some small uses, i.e. clouding a door or lock myself into a drawer and cloud it, but that doesn\u00b4t seem that useful at all. So there\u00b4s a great chance that I don\u00b4t get it immediate use, maybe you know more.<br /> <br /> Then there\u00b4s something puzzling about Obfuscate 3, it says &quot;Used with Cloak of night, touch of shadow can now affect other people&quot;, is that a typo and it is the other way around? Because in Touch of shadow, it reads &quot;... in the case of an unwilling victim, the vampire must roll to touch his opponent&quot;, indicating that you can use it on other people already at Obfuscate 2.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the help and keep on gaming,<br /> <br /> Dennis <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T10:48:55-07:00","id":1129295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Narr666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129278-please-educate-me-on-obfuscate#post1129278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the about Obfuscate 2: I have got a rule: When in games an ability looks particularly weak there\u00b4s a great chance that you haven\u00b4t understood it. I mean, carrying stuff around can be done with 1. So it\u00b4s only really useful when you cloud an object that you aren\u00b4t touching. But since it only begins to work when you touch it and it only is active for a scene, you must be present and touch this thing before. I can imagine some small uses, i.e. clouding a door or lock myself into a drawer and cloud it, but that doesn\u00b4t seem that useful at all. So there\u00b4s a great chance that I don\u00b4t get it immediate use, maybe you know more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disappearing doors are AMAZING. (Also terrifying if the person really needs an exit, say like you're trying to set up a murder-box for example) <br /> Outside of offensive murder-box applications it also is good at hiding the doors you just passed through to help with escaping in a Chase scene.<br /> Obfuscated ghouled animals can make for a bad night as they are only going to be Blood Bond to their master and are likely Vitae Addicted (aka literally blood thirsty). (\u2022 Retainer - Ghouled Guard Dog [<b>Discipline: </b>Varies <b>Field: </b>Murdering Intruders])<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T10:57:40-07:00","id":1129299,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate 1 only works where people expect to see <i>someone</i>. The details are obscured, so you can walk down a street carrying a machine gun without issue, but if you're alone in someone's apartment they'll see you. True invisibility requires obfuscate 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T10:59:18-07:00","id":1129301,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate is more than just invisibility. It's a type of subtle mind control.<br /> <br /> Its basic function compels the person to <i>ignore your presence</i>, unless you do something that overtly draws their attention to yourself, such as combat, or destroying the environment. People will subconsciously walk around you (instead of into you), and they'll block out any normal audio made by those protected under the effects of Obfuscate. Though screaming at the top of your lungs, or setting off a bomb might break the illusion.<br /> <br /> <br /> And yes, there are more advanced powers of Obfuscate which can allow the vampire to look like somebody else. So you could be standing in a room in full view of everybody, but they wouldn't see the vampire. They'd see whoever the vampire was trying to impersonate.<br /> <br /> As for using it on other people, I believe it means you can simultaneously affect an entire group. As in, you wave your hands and make 2 or more people vanish from everybody's collective notice.<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, you need to keep in mind that the clans who have a natural affinity for Obfuscate are the Nosferatu and the Mekhet, two clans who have a reputation for secrecy and manipulation. <i>Obfuscate's main purpose is espionage</i>. So hiding yourself inside a drawer and going unnoticed would be extremely useful if you're doing a 'fly on the wall' scenario. You could be standing right next to your enemy, listening to their private conversations and they wouldn't even know about it!<br /> <br /> As for small objects, you could sneak a tool or a weapon past security and give it to a captive prisoner, or you might abscond with evidence vital to an investigation and cause the case to go cold. You could steal a priceless artifact or treasure and walk right out the front door. All kinds of super spy level behavior can be done by hiding small objects on your person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-15-2017, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T11:03:42-07:00","id":1129303,"title":"","content":"The &quot;use on other people thing&quot; allows you to use touch of shadows on <i>humans</i>. With two dots it only works on objects and animals (who may be the unwilling subjects referred to in the text).<br /> <br /> If you want to affect multiple people that's a devotion, Cloak the Gathering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T11:13:47-07:00","id":1129307,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers, but I certainly wasn\u00b4t clear enough what I liked to know. I was asking specifically on<u> Obfuscate 1:</u><br /> <br /> <i>W</i>hat happens when I use Obfuscate 1 when and someone comes in: Does Obfuscate fail or will he roll Wits + Composure - Obfuscate. And if he fails that roll, what then? Does he sees &quot;someone&quot; but can\u00b4t remember him? Or does he sees someone and recognizes him until he went out of the room and then his memory is clouded?<br /> And when he comes into his room, makes his roll and fails, what happens when that Vampire talks with him. Does he talk to someone he does not recognize? What happens if he knows that Vampire he\u00b4s speaking to? Would he not recognize him?<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> <br /> Dennis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T11:18:31-07:00","id":1129310,"title":"","content":"To quote the discipline: &quot;Unless the vampire\u2019s doing something to draw people\u2019s attention \u2014 pulling a gun, or screaming at people \u2014 <b>or he\u2019s in a place where someone doesn\u2019t expect anyone else to be</b>, everyone around him ignores him.&quot;<br /> <br /> So if you're in someone's apartment and there's not a party going on, obfuscate will fail and the owner will notice you. Obfuscate <i>3</i>, which provides true invisibility, is required to be unseen here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T11:20:04-07:00","id":1129313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129278-please-educate-me-on-obfuscate?p=1129310#post1129310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To quote the discipline: &quot;Unless the vampire\u2019s doing something to draw people\u2019s attention \u2014 pulling a gun, or screaming at people \u2014 <b>or he\u2019s in a place where someone doesn\u2019t expect anyone else to be</b>, everyone around him ignores him.&quot;<br /> <br /> So if you're in someone's apartment and there's not a party going on, obfuscate will fail and the owner will notice you.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it fails, that makes sense. Thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T11:34:46-07:00","id":1129321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Narr666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129278-please-educate-me-on-obfuscate?p=1129307#post1129307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>W</i>hat happens when I use Obfuscate 1 when and someone comes in: Does Obfuscate fail or will he roll Wits + Composure - Obfuscate. And if he fails that roll, what then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate fails. The thing to remember about Obfuscate 1 is that it works by making people not pay attention to you, because you're &quot;just some guy/gal.&quot; It stops working when people start to pay attention to you. If you walk into someone's bedroom looking like &quot;just some guy&quot;, you are inherently calling attention to yourself, unless the person was expecting &quot;some guy&quot; to come into their bedroom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Narr666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129278-please-educate-me-on-obfuscate?p=1129307#post1129307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does he sees &quot;someone&quot; but can\u00b4t remember him? Or does he sees someone and recognizes him until he went out of the room and then his memory is clouded?</div> </div> </div> </div>He sees a random, unimportant person walk into his room. This being a rather unexpected and alarming turn of events, he would likely try to figure out who this random guy is that just walked into his bedroom. At this point, he is paying attention to the vampire, so Obfuscate 1 stops working.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Narr666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129278-please-educate-me-on-obfuscate?p=1129307#post1129307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And when he comes into his room, makes his roll and fails, what happens when that Vampire talks with him. Does he talk to someone he does not recognize? What happens if he knows that Vampire he\u00b4s speaking to? Would he not recognize him?</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking the bedroom part out of the example, if a vampire using Obfuscate 1 starts talking to him, that might or might not break Obfuscate, depending on the context of the conversation. If you're in a public place and some random stranger asks you for the time, you don't pay them that much attention. You might answer or tell them you don't know, or ignore them depending on how receptive you are to strangers. But if instead of asking for the time they ask for your social security number, you're probably going to want to figure out who this person is that's asking you for personal information. That would break Obfuscate 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-15-2017, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T12:31:10-07:00","id":1129358,"title":"","content":"Thx a lot. That makes sense. I\u00b4m still not sold on Obf.2, but I will see what my players do with it and maybe that will change my mind.<br /> <br /> Keep on gaming,<br /> <br /> Dennis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T13:42:36-07:00","id":1129400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Narr666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129278-please-educate-me-on-obfuscate?p=1129358#post1129358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thx a lot. That makes sense. I\u00b4m still not sold on Obf.2, but I will see what my players do with it and maybe that will change my mind.<br /> <br /> Keep on gaming,<br /> <br /> Dennis</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the main uses I've seen for Ob 2 is concealing weapons and contraband on one's person. Granted, you can achieve this using Obfuscate 1, but only by making your entire person seemingly unimportant, which is not always desirable or practical. For example, if the city has a law forbidding weapons in Elysium, and you want to smuggle one past the Prince's security, Ob 1 won't cut it. The security guards aren't going to allow &quot;some guy&quot; into Elysium, whether they notice the weapons he's carrying or not. So instead, you go in as Victor the Mekhet, and you make your weapons look like &quot;just some junk.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then there's the old Ob 2 on the door trick, which has a couple neat applications. Or if you want to hide a body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}